ref="/docs/math-random/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID / DATA &amp; BEHAVIOR</p><h1 class="page-title">Dictionaries</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Associate keys and values while preserving insertion order.</p><p>Complete program for the synchronous entry adapter. The result below is the returned integer.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>dictionaries.void<a href="/docs/snippets/dictionaries.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="dictionaries.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/dictionaries.void"><span class="keyword">func</span> entry(extra_notebooks: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
