     supplies[<span class="string">&quot;notebooks&quot;</span>] += extra_notebooks
     <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="keyword">match</span> supplies.get(<span class="string">&quot;notebooks&quot;</span>):
         Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> quantity): quantity
-        Err(<span class="keyword">var</span> reason): <span class="number">0</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/dictionaries.void" data-input="5" data-expected="7">Input <strong>5</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>7</strong></div></figure><section id="part-1"><h2>Create a typed mapping</h2><p><code>{string: i32}</code> maps supply names to quantities. The literal starts with two notebooks and five pens. Looking up <code>supplies["notebooks"]</code> yields the quantity for that known key.</p></section><section id="part-2"><h2>Update and insert</h2><p>Compound assignment adds the input to an existing notebook quantity; input <code>5</code> gives <code>7</code>. Assigning a value to a new key inserts it. The program uses <code>get("notebooks")</code> to handle lookup as a result. Direct indexing and compound assignment require the key to exist; missing keys raise a runtime failure. Use <code>contains(key)</code> to test presence, or <code>get(key)</code> to obtain <code>Ok(value)</code> or <code>Err("key not found")</code>. This example chooses zero if the key is missing.</p></section><section id="part-3"><h2>Explore membership and order</h2><p>Iteration uses <code>for quantity, name in supplies:</code> in insertion order; <code>reverse</code> visits the reverse order. Replacing a value preserves its key’s position. <code>remove(key)</code> reports whether removal happened, while <code>clear()</code> empties the mapping. Assignment shares dictionary identity. Recoverable lookup preserves the value type and its readonly restrictions.</p></section><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a><a href="/examples/">Explore examples</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#part-1">Create a typed mapping</a><a href="#part-2">Update and insert</a><a href="#part-3">Explore membership and order</a></nav><