D / TOOLING &amp; INTEGRATION</p><h1 class="page-title">Editor tooling & diagnostics</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Keep feedback close to the code you wrote.</p><p>Illustrative function fragment. Use <code>reading_total(reading, count)</code> as a small source-navigation target: its declaration names both parameters and its return type. This function returns their product; it does not assert that a particular completion or hover UI is already distributed.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>editor-tooling.void<a href="/docs/snippets/editor-tooling.void" download>Download fragment</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="editor-tooling.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/editor-tooling.void"><span class="keyword">func</span> reading_total(reading: <span class="keyword">i32</span>, count: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
-    <span class="keyword">return</span> reading * count</code></pre></figure><section id="part-1"><h2>Understand source, not backend machinery</h2><p>VOID’s diagnostic direction is clear .void locations, useful ranges and explanations that refer to language concepts. Normal errors should not require understanding generated LLVM IR, mangled symbols or linker internals.</p></section><section id="part-2"><h2>One language service</h2><p>The shared language server uses compiler-owned analysis for diagnostics and navigation. Implemented queries include completion, hover, signature help, symbols and guarded editing operations across editor integrations. These capabilities are still in development, with no public editor builds distributed here.</p></section><section id="part-3"><h2>Edits need semantic boundaries</h2><p>Rename and formatting deliberately operate on supported cases. Rename is not a universal operation on every declaration kind. Formatting is conservative rather than a full reflow or import-sorting system. Semantic highlighting and general code actions are not promised by the current server.</p></section><section id="part-4"><h2>The experience being built</h2><p>The goal is a useful everyday editor: quick answers about types and parameters, navigation that follows actual declarations, and feedback that stays attached to current source. Package discovery belongs to the future ecosystem; a native package manager is not available.</p></section><section id="current-tooling"><h2>Source-aware assistance, shared across editors</h2><p>Completion, documentation hover, parameter help, definitions, references, document/workspace symbols, guarded rename and conservative formatting are implemented through compiler-owned analysis. Module completion follows the selected source graph, including nested import paths. <code>##</code> documentation comments and <code>## @param</code> descriptions supply authored help. References inside string interpolation retain their source locations.</p><p>VS Code and Neovim provide adapters for the shared server; Vim uses yegappan/lsp with rename disabled. Existing integrations have local Linux execution evidence. VSCodium is a compatibility target with execution unverified; the newest language assistance still needs fresh interactive-client validation. Broader Windows/macOS combinations and clean-machine distribution remain unverified. Installed standard sources are protected from rename and formatting.</p></section><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a><a href="/why-void/">Why VOID</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#part-1">Understand source, not backend machinery</a><a href="#part-2">One language service</a><a href="#part-3">Edits need semantic boundaries</a><a href="#part-4">The experience being built</a><a href="#current-tooling">Source-aware assistance, shared across editors</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="https://github.com/Shmellyorc/Void.Language">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
