     <span class="keyword">return</span> items * rates.unit_price()</code></pre></figure><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>delivery.void<a href="/docs/snippets/modules/delivery.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="delivery.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/modules/delivery.void"><span class="keyword">func</span> delivery_fee() -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
     <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="number">3</span></code></pre></figure></section><section id="part-2"><h2>Use qualified and direct names</h2><p>The absolute project-root import is aliased as <code>pricing</code>, so its function is called as <code>pricing.subtotal</code>. The relative delivery import exposes its unambiguous name directly. Five items at four plus delivery of three return <code>23</code>.</p></section><section id="part-3"><h2>Read paths in project context</h2><p>A leading slash refers to the virtual project root, not the operating-system root. A quoted path, with or without <code>./</code>, resolves from the importing file. Exact-case <code>.void</code> filenames and forward slashes are required. Parent paths remain bounded by the project root; a package manager is not supplied.</p></section><section id="nested-imports"><h2>Follow paths from the importing file</h2><p><code>use "details/rates.void" as rates</code> inside pricing resolves from that file’s directory, just like <code>./details/rates.void</code>. Keep the directory when downloading this supporting module.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>rates.void<a href="/docs/snippets/modules/details/rates.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="rates.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/modules/details/rates.void"><span class="keyword">func</span> unit_price() -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
-    <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="number">4</span></code></pre></figure><p>Unquoted <code>use io/files as files</code> illustrates nested standard-source spelling. It resolves <code>io/files.void</code> under the compiler’s selected standard-source root. An absolute <code>VOID_STDLIB_ROOT</code> override can select that root; otherwise the compiler’s configured source root is used. This is syntax only: no shipped <code>io/files</code> module or filesystem API is promised. Standard sources cannot import quoted project files. Importing a native provider never grants host trust.</p></section><section id="entry-discovery"><h2>Find the project entry deliberately</h2><p>With a compatible local compiler, <code>voidc run . --app</code> discovers <code>main.void</code>. Directory-based <code>check</code> and <code>emit</code> use the same discovery. From an active file, discovery looks for the nearest exact <code>main.void</code> through parent directories up to the workspace boundary. Without an active file, only the workspace root is checked; there is no recursive search. An explicitly selected entry wins, source errors never trigger a fallback, and the selected entry remains fixed during a session until deliberately changed or restarted.</p><p>The complete source above uses the legacy <code>entry(i32)</code> adapter: run it with a numeric input, not <code>--app</code>. See <a href="/docs/syntax/#application">application entry</a> for a main-based program. These workflows describe implemented compiler behavior, not a public download or installation command.</p></section><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a><a href="/examples/#modules">Explore examples</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#part-1">Keep the module paths together</a><a href="#part-2">Use qualified and direct names</a><a href="#part-3">Read paths in project context</a><a href="#nested-imports">Follow paths from the importing file</a><a href="#entry-discovery">Find the project entry deliberately</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="https://github.com/Shmellyorc/Void.Language">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
