ref="/docs/math-random/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID / DATA &amp; BEHAVIOR</p><h1 class="page-title">Strings & Unicode</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Use one text type throughout ordinary code.</p><p>Illustrative fragment — place this code inside a function. It is verified in an executable context, but the download is not a standalone program.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>strings.void<a href="/docs/snippets/strings.void" download>Download fragment</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="strings.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/strings.void"><span class="keyword">const</span> name = <span class="string">&quot;世界&quot;</span>
 <span class="keyword">var</span> message = <span class="string">&quot;Hello, {name}!&quot;</span></code></pre></figure><section id="part-1"><h2>Create and combine text</h2><p>The local fragment inserts a string name into a greeting. The value is <code>"Hello, 世界!"</code>. Interpolation needs no prefix: <code>"{name}"</code> evaluates its string expression once. Use <code>{{</code> and <code>}}</code> for literal braces. Numeric, Boolean and custom-value interpolation, format specifications and multiline string literals remain future work. This fragment does not print anything.</p></section><section id="part-2"><h2>Rebind without changing earlier text</h2><p>String content is immutable; assignment can share that content safely. Concatenation with <code>+</code> creates combined text; <code>+=</code> rebinds a mutable string without changing earlier text. A defaultable uninitialized string local or field starts empty.</p></section><section id="part-3"><h2>Understand Unicode and API limits</h2><p>Strings compare exact UTF-8 content without Unicode normalization. Supported escapes include <code>\n</code>, <code>\t</code> and scalar escapes such as <code>\u{e9}</code>. <code>text.length</code> counts Unicode scalars; <code>text.byte_length</code> counts UTF-8 bytes, both as <code>i64</code>. <code>text[index]</code> returns a one-scalar string and accepts negative indexes. It raises a checked failure out of bounds. Scalars are not grapheme clusters: combining marks can count separately. Printing and automatic numeric conversion are not supplied by these operations.</p></section><section id="utf8"><h2>Convert UTF-8 explicitly</h2><p><code>"café"</code> has four scalars and five UTF-8 bytes. <code>to_utf8()</code> creates an independent owned byte list. <code>string.from_utf8(bytes)</code> copies and validates bytes, returning <code>result&lt;string, string&gt;</code>; invalid input returns <code>Err("invalid UTF-8")</code>. This program returns the decoded scalar count. The adapter input is unused.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>utf8.void<a href="/docs/snippets/utf8.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="utf8.void source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/utf8.void"><span class="keyword">func</span> entry(input: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
     <span class="keyword">var</span> bytes = <span class="string">&quot;café&quot;</span>.to_utf8()
     <span class="keyword">var</span> decoded = <span class="keyword">string</span>.from_utf8(bytes)
     <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="keyword">match</span> decoded:
         Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> text): text.length as <span class="keyword">i32</span>
-        Err(<span class="keyword">var</span> reason): <span class="number">0</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/utf8.void" data-input="0" data-expected="4">Input <strong>0</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>4</strong></div></figure></section><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a><a href="/examples/">Explore examples</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#part-1">Create and combine text</a><a href="#part-2">Rebind without changing earlier text</a><a href="#part-3">Understand Unicode and API limits</a><a href="#utf8">Convert UTF-8 explicitly</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="https://github.com/Shmellyorc/Void.Language">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
