-    <span class="keyword">return</span> total_lines</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/task-groups.void" data-input="5" data-expected="240">Input <strong>5</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>240</strong></div></figure><section id="part-1"><h2>Give chapter work one scope</h2><p>The group owns the two <code>line_count</code> tasks created inside it. Each uses a fixed forty-lines-per-page model, so the chapter and one-page appendix have independent integer results. No shared counter is mutated.</p></section><section id="part-2"><h2>Keep the result outside the group</h2><p>Declare <code>total_lines</code> outside the group so it is available afterward. The parent explicitly awaits both results; normal scope exit also joins any remaining children. Input <code>5</code> gives <code>200 + 40 = 240</code>. The group alias is lexical, not a first-class collection or a <code>jobs.spawn</code> API.</p></section><section id="part-3"><h2>Understand early exits</h2><p>Early exits from nested scopes request cooperative cancellation of unfinished work and join it before leaving. Dropping a handle never detaches a task. This example shows successful completion through the explicit async host adapter; it does not demonstrate cancellation recovery or change the ordinary CLI adapter.</p></section><section id="completed-tasks"><h2>What completion releases</h2><p>After a task’s owning resume returns, or its worker completion is safely acquired, the runtime releases the completed execution frame’s GC root. Objects reachable only from that frame can then be collected. A caller can still await the retained result.</p><p>This improves frame reclamation; it does not make async execution constant-memory. Result objects, task and worker records, group records, handle registrations and retained capacities can still grow with the total tasks created within a root execution. Structured scopes and precise GC do not replace those lifetime boundaries.</p></section><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a><a href="/examples/#task-groups">Explore examples</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#part-1">Give chapter work one scope</a><a href="#part-2">Keep the result outside the group</a><a href="#part-3">Understand early exits</a><a href="#completed-tasks">What completion releases</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="https://github.com/Shmellyorc/Void.Language">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
