-<section class="section container why-direction" aria-labelledby="tooling-title"><p class="eyebrow">FEEDBACK THAT UNDERSTANDS YOUR CODE</p><h2 id="tooling-title">One language service.<br><span class="gradient">Closer to your ideas.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">Editor feedback comes from the compiler’s understanding of VOID source, so navigation and code intelligence follow the language’s own rules.</p><div class="direction-grid"><article><h3>Understand. Navigate. Refine.</h3><p>Completion, hover information, signature help, definitions and references, and document and workspace symbols are implemented in the compiler-owned language server. Project queries follow the selected entry’s reachable source graph. Nearest-main discovery and nested module paths keep that context explicit; documentation comments and interpolation references stay tied to source.</p><p>Guarded rename covers supported functions and bindings. Conservative four-space formatting preserves tokens, comments and imports; it does not promise a full reflow or general code actions.</p><a class="roadmap-link" href="/docs/editor-tooling/">Explore editor tooling <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article><h3>Meet your editor where it is.</h3><p>VS Code and Neovim adapters include guards for version-sensitive edits. Vim uses yegappan/lsp for the shared language service, with rename disabled because its edit-safety contract differs.</p><p>These integrations have local Linux execution evidence. VSCodium is an integration target with execution still unverified. New Windows/macOS editor combinations and clean-machine distribution also remain unverified.</p><a class="roadmap-link" href="/roadmap/#current-development">See current development <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div><div class="guide-note"><strong>Implemented locally; broader validation is pending.</strong><p>New capabilities are locally verified; broader platform and fresh interactive-editor validation are ongoing. No public compiler or editor builds are distributed here.</p></div></section>
