+<main id="main" class="inner-page"><section class="section tinted"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">THE ROAD AHEAD</p><div class="section-heading"><h1 class="page-title">VOID Language roadmap.<br><span class="gradient">A clear direction.</span></h1><p>VOID is in active development. Here is what works, what is being improved and where the language is heading. No dates or completion percentages are promised.</p></div><div class="topic-jump"><a href="#foundation">Implemented foundation</a><a href="#platforms">Hosted verification</a><a href="#current-development">Work under verification</a><a href="#limits">Known limits</a><a href="#future">Future direction</a></div></div></section><section class="section container feature-explanations" aria-label="Roadmap priorities"><article id="foundation"><span class="status implemented">Implemented foundation</span><h2>Programs, data and native execution</h2><p>The compiler uses C++20 and LLVM/Clang/LLD 23.1.4. One lowering pipeline serves JIT execution and native object emission. Applications support main or top-level execution, file globals and ordered initialization. The numeric entry adapter remains available for small calculations.</p><p><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Run and build an application</a></p></article><article id="platforms"><span class="status implemented">Verified on hosted systems</span><h2>Compiler, Runtime and editor coverage</h2><p>Compiler and Runtime suites have run on Ubuntu, Windows Server and macOS ARM64, including strict sanitizers on Ubuntu. VS Code integration runs against the real language server. The standard library includes math, random, collections, text encodings, binary streams, files, paths, OS queries and channels.</p><p><a href="/docs/">Browse all guides</a></p></article><article id="current-development"><span class="status implemented">Implemented · verification open</span><h2>Networking and logging</h2><p>HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, TLS verification, async DNS, uploads, redirects and streaming are implemented. Linux and macOS passed the hosted HTTP suites. Windows passed 340 of 341 tests in the relevant run. The remaining failure concerns explicit P12 client identity with Schannel. Logging has cross-platform functional coverage, while its performance review and release hold remain open after an unresolved optimizer incident.</p><p><a href="/docs/url-http/">Read about HTTP ownership</a> · <a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a></p></article><article id="limits"><span class="status implemented">Known limits</span><h2>Resources and interoperability</h2><p>Runtime admission bounds network resources. Application-held response data and operating-system trust services have different memory costs. Native workers require supported value transfers. External native bindings require a trusted host. Clean-machine distribution and some editor combinations still need validation.</p><p><a href="/docs/native-integration/">Native integration</a></p></article><article id="future"><span class="status implemented">Future direction</span><h2>Packages and the development loop</h2><p>Future work includes package discovery, broader typed native integration and a save-driven live workflow. Function-body replacement already exists in Runtime integration; automated watching and compatibility across arbitrary changes are separate goals. Public release timing is open.</p><p><a href="/docs/live-development/">Live development</a></p></article></section><section class="closing container"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE WHAT WORKS TODAY</p><h2>Start with <span class="gradient">the language.</span></h2></div><a class="button primary" href="/examples/">Explore VOID</a></section></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
