+    <span class="keyword">return</span> packet[<span class="number">0</span>] <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i32</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/binary-memory.void" data-input="258" data-expected="1">Input <strong>258</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>1</strong></div></figure><section id="order"><h2>Read the first byte</h2><p>Encoding the unsigned value 258 in big-endian order gives bytes 1 and 2. The example returns the first byte. Include width and byte order in a file format so a reader on another machine can decode it.</p></section><section id="cursor"><h2>Use a memory cursor</h2><p><code>use io/memory as memory</code> supplies <code>memory.stream()</code>. Write typed values, seek back to the beginning and read using the same order. These operations return results. Check a failed seek or short read before using its value.</p></section><section id="copy"><h2>Keep an independent snapshot</h2><p><code>to_bytes()</code> returns a copy of the stream contents. Use <code>read_exact(count)</code> for fixed-size fields and <code>read_bytes(max_count)</code> when a shorter block is acceptable.</p></section><section id="read-field"><h2>Decode from a cursor</h2><p>The stream starts at offset zero with little-endian order. Reading two bytes advances the cursor. A low byte of two and a high byte of one represent 258.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>read-field.void<a href="/docs/snippets/read-field.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="read-field source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/read-field.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> io/memory <span class="keyword">as</span> memory
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(low_byte: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> field: [<span class="keyword">u8</span>] = [low_byte <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">u8</span>, <span class="number">1</span>]
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> packet = memory.stream(field)
+    <span class="keyword">if</span> packet.read&lt;<span class="keyword">u16</span>&gt;() <span class="keyword">is</span> Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> number):
+        <span class="keyword">return</span> number <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i32</span>
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> -<span class="number">1</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/read-field.void" data-input="2" data-expected="258">Input <strong>2</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>258</strong></div></figure></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and paths</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#order">Read the first byte</a><a href="#cursor">Use a memory cursor</a><a href="#copy">Keep an independent snapshot</a><a href="#read-field">Decode from a cursor</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
