om/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/" aria-current="page">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID</p><h1 class="page-title">Topic subscriptions</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Deliver a typed notification to a subscriber and disconnect it by handle.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>channels.void<a href="/docs/snippets/channels.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Topic subscriptions source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/channels.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> channel
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(count: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> updates = channel.router&lt;<span class="keyword">i32</span>&gt;()
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> displayed: <span class="keyword">i32</span> = <span class="number">0</span>
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> token = updates.subscribe(<span class="string">&quot;stock&quot;</span>, <span class="keyword">func</span>(<span class="keyword">const</span> quantity: <span class="keyword">i32</span>):
+        displayed = quantity
+    )
+    updates.emit(<span class="string">&quot;stock&quot;</span>, count)
+    updates.unsubscribe(token)
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> displayed</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/channels.void" data-input="9" data-expected="9">Input <strong>9</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>9</strong></div></figure><section id="emit"><h2>Send one update</h2><p>A <code>channel.router&lt;i32&gt;</code> delivers one payload type. A callback captures the local display value. Emitting a count on the matching topic updates it before <code>emit</code> returns.</p></section><section id="token"><h2>Own the subscription</h2><p>Store the subscription returned by <code>subscribe</code>, then pass that token to the same router to unsubscribe. Dropping a token alone does not disconnect its handler. <code>clear()</code> removes registrations and the router can be reused.</p></section><section id="thread"><h2>Deliver on the owning thread</h2><p>Delivery is synchronous in registration order. A router is managed, so assignments share subscriptions. Use it on its owning application thread. Worker communication requires a different ownership model.</p></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/events/">Events</a> · <a href="/docs/closures/">Closures</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#emit">Send one update</a><a href="#token">Own the subscription</a><a href="#thread">Deliver on the owning thread</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
