om/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/" aria-current="page">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID</p><h1 class="page-title">Collection helpers</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Transform and search lists while keeping the original ordering available.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>collection-tools.void<a href="/docs/snippets/collection-tools.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Collection helpers source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/collection-tools.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> collections
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(last_stop: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> stops: [<span class="keyword">i32</span>] = [<span class="number">12</span>, <span class="number">8</span>, last_stop]
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> newest = collections.reversed(stops)
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> newest[<span class="number">0</span>]</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/collection-tools.void" data-input="21" data-expected="21">Input <strong>21</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>21</strong></div></figure><section id="copy"><h2>Get a fresh list</h2><p>With <code>use collections</code>, <code>reversed</code> returns a fresh outer list. Our delivery queue ends with the newest stop. Reading the first element of its reversed copy returns that stop without changing the queue.</p></section><section id="sort"><h2>Sort and search</h2><p>Pass the same ordering to <code>sorted</code> and <code>binary_search</code>. Searching requires an already sorted list. Match the search result to distinguish a missing value from a valid index of zero.</p></section><section id="identity"><h2>Understand copies</h2><p>Reordering creates new list storage. If elements reference managed objects, the copies still refer to those objects. For insertion-ordered key/value lookup, see <a href="/docs/dictionaries/">Dictionaries</a>.</p></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/dictionaries/">Dictionaries</a> · <a href="/docs/generics/">Generics</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#copy">Get a fresh list</a><a href="#sort">Sort and search</a><a href="#identity">Understand copies</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/"