om/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/" aria-current="page">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID</p><h1 class="page-title">Files and host paths</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Extract a filename and handle a filesystem operation through its result.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>files-paths.void<a href="/docs/snippets/files-paths.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Files and host paths source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/files-paths.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> path
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(offset: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">if</span> path.filename(<span class="string">&quot;atlas/map.txt&quot;</span>) is Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> name):
+        <span class="keyword">return</span> (name.length <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i32</span>) + offset
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="number">0</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/files-paths.void" data-input="0" data-expected="7">Input <strong>0</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>7</strong></div></figure><section id="filename"><h2>Separate the filename</h2><p>This example asks for the filename in a relative path. It needs no existing file. The name “map.txt” has seven scalars. A failed path operation returns an error, handled here by returning zero.</p></section><section id="open"><h2>Open a file deliberately</h2><p><code>use io</code> provides <code>io.open(path, io.open_mode.read)</code>. Match the result before using the file. <code>read_bytes</code> allows short reads. <code>read_exact</code> asks for an exact byte count.</p></section><section id="close"><h2>Finish using the handle</h2><p>Use <code>close()</code> when the outcome matters, or scoped <code>with</code> for deterministic cleanup. Do not rely on garbage collection to close files. Inspect the returned I/O error for operation, path and partial progress. Host path syntax and separators depend on platform.</p></section><section id="read-field"><h2>Read a fixed-size field</h2><p>Set <code>VOID_GUIDE_FILE</code> to a three-byte file. Asking for two bytes returns two. Asking for four returns the example’s failure value, −1. The <code>with</code> scope releases the handle on both paths.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>count-bytes.void<a href="/docs/snippets/count-bytes.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="count-bytes source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/count-bytes.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> io
+<span class="keyword">use</span> os
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> sample_size(filename: <span class="keyword">string</span>, wanted: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">result</span>&lt;<span class="keyword">i32</span>, io.error&gt;:
+    <span class="keyword">with</span> io.open(filename)? <span class="keyword">as</span> handle:
+        <span class="keyword">var</span> block = handle.read_exact(wanted <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i64</span>)?
+        <span class="keyword">return</span> Ok(block.count <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i32</span>)
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(wanted: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">if</span> os.env(<span class="string">&quot;VOID_GUIDE_FILE&quot;</span>) <span class="keyword">is</span> Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> filename):
+        <span class="keyword">if</span> sample_size(filename, wanted) <span class="keyword">is</span> Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> count):
+            <span class="keyword">return</span> count
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> -<span class="number">1</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/count-bytes.void" data-input="2" data-expected="2">Input <strong>2</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>2</strong></div></figure></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/os-directories/">Application directories</a> · <a href="/docs/errors/">Results and errors</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#filename">Separate the filename</a><a href="#open">Open a file deliberately</a><a href="#close">Finish using the handle</a><a href="#read-field">Read a fixed-size field</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
