+    <span class="keyword">if</span> settings.minimum is log.level.warn:
+        <span class="keyword">return</span> count
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="number">0</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/logging.void" data-input="6" data-expected="6">Input <strong>6</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>6</strong></div></figure><section id="threshold"><h2>Choose which records qualify</h2><p><code>log.config</code> is a value record. A warning threshold admits warnings and errors. This example inspects the configuration without writing a file or console record.</p></section><section id="output"><h2>Own the logger</h2><p><code>log.open(options)</code> returns a result containing a logger or a failure. Check the results of <code>write</code>, <code>flush</code> and <code>close</code>. <code>write_lazy</code> lets a logger avoid constructing a message when its level is disabled.</p></section><section id="limits"><h2>Configure rotation deliberately</h2><p>File logging uses an explicit path, byte limit and backup count. Existing filenames require explicit adoption in an exclusive-writer directory. The logging API has passed cross-platform tests. Its performance review remains open and release is on hold following an unresolved compiler optimizer incident.</p></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/files-paths/">File ownership</a> · <a href="/docs/errors/">Error handling</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#threshold">Choose which records qualify</a><a href="#output">Own the logger</a><a href="#limits">Configure rotation deliberately</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>