+    <span class="keyword">return</span> math.clamp(score, <span class="number">0</span>, <span class="number">10</span>)</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/math-random.void" data-input="14" data-expected="10">Input <strong>14</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>10</strong></div></figure><section id="bounds"><h2>Keep a score within bounds</h2><p>Import <code>math</code> for typed numeric helpers. Here the scoreboard accepts values from zero to ten. Passing 14 returns 10. The same clamp returns its input when it already lies between the bounds.</p></section><section id="sequence"><h2>Reproduce a draw</h2><p>With <code>use random</code>, construct <code>random.generator(42)</code> for deterministic draws. A generator is a value. Copying it copies its current sequence position. Give separate simulations their own generators when their draws should be independent.</p></section><section id="errors"><h2>Choose a fallible operation</h2><p>Use <code>try_rand_range</code> when bounds come from input and match its result before using the draw. Use the seeded generator for simulations and reproducible tests. It provides no cryptographic secrecy.</p></section><section id="try-it"><h2>Try the operation</h2><p>Both generators begin in the same state. The integer interval includes one and six. Replaying a draw with the same seed gives the same face.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>replay-draw.void<a href="/docs/snippets/replay-draw.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="replay-draw source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/replay-draw.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> random
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(game_number: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> first = random.generator(game_number <span class="keyword">as</span> u64)
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> replay = first
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> chosen = first.rand_range(<span class="number">1</span>, <span class="number">6</span>)
+    <span class="keyword">if</span> replay.rand_range(<span class="number">1</span>, <span class="number">6</span>) == chosen:
+        <span class="keyword">return</span> chosen
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="number">0</span></code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/replay-draw.void" data-input="8" data-expected="5">Input <strong>8</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>5</strong></div></figure></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#bounds">Keep a score within bounds</a><a href="#sequence">Reproduce a draw</a><a href="#errors">Choose a fallible operation</a><a href="#try-it">Try the operation</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
