om/">Math and seeded random numbers</a><a href="/docs/collection-tools/">Collection helpers</a><a href="/docs/text-encoding/">Text and byte encodings</a><a href="/docs/binary-memory/">Binary values and memory streams</a><a href="/docs/files-paths/">Files and host paths</a><a href="/docs/os-directories/">Platform information and directories</a><a href="/docs/logging/">Logging</a><a href="/docs/channels/">Topic subscriptions</a><a href="/docs/url-http/" aria-current="page">URLs and HTTP clients</a><a href="/docs/compiler-workflow/">Running and building applications</a><a href="/docs/console-output/">Writing to the console</a><a href="/docs/json-data/">Reading JSON data</a><a href="/docs/calendar-time/">Dates and clocks</a></details></nav></aside><article class="guide-article"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN VOID</p><h1 class="page-title">URLs and HTTP clients</h1><p class="guide-tagline">Encode a query component, then choose buffered or streamed HTTP responses.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>url-http.void<a href="/docs/snippets/url-http.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="URLs and HTTP clients source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/url-http.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> url
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(extra: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">var</span> escaped = url.encode_component(<span class="string">&quot;a b&quot;</span>)
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> (escaped.length <span class="keyword">as</span> <span class="keyword">i32</span>) + extra</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/url-http.void" data-input="0" data-expected="5">Input <strong>0</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>5</strong></div></figure><section id="component"><h2>Encode one value</h2><p><code>url.encode_component("a b")</code> gives <code>a%20b</code>. Its five ASCII characters can be counted without opening a connection. Use <code>url.parse</code> for explicit HTTP(S) addresses and <code>url.resolve</code> for relative references. Both return typed errors.</p></section><section id="client"><h2>Own requests and responses</h2><p>Import <code>net/http as http</code>. <code>http.open_client()</code> returns a client or an error. A client owns its connection pool. Use <code>get</code> or <code>send</code> for a bounded buffered response. An HTTP error status such as 404 is still a response. Inspect its status separately from a DNS, TLS or timeout error.</p></section><section id="stream"><h2>Read incrementally</h2><p>Use <code>client.start</code> and read chunks for large bodies. Consume and release each chunk to keep application memory bounded. Deterministically close transfers and clients. Cancellation cannot retract a request already received by the server.</p></section><section id="verification"><h2>Platform verification</h2><p>The implementation supports HTTP/1.1, negotiated HTTP/2, TLS peer and hostname verification, proxy options and explicit client identity. Linux and macOS passed hosted suites. Windows Schannel P12 client authentication remains unresolved. Full HTTP acceptance is pending.</p></section><section id="try-it"><h2>Try the operation</h2><p>Set <code>VOID_GUIDE_URL</code> to a local HTTP server that returns status 200. The sample reads the received status. If lookup or transport fails, it returns the input fallback. Verification serves a loopback response for each execution.</p><figure class="guide-code"><figcaption>read-status.void<a href="/docs/snippets/read-status.void" download>Download source</a></figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="read-status source"><code data-source="/docs/snippets/read-status.void"><span class="keyword">use</span> os
+<span class="keyword">use</span> net/http <span class="keyword">as</span> http
+
+<span class="keyword">func</span> entry(fallback: <span class="keyword">i32</span>) -&gt; <span class="keyword">i32</span>:
+    <span class="keyword">if</span> os.env(<span class="string">&quot;VOID_GUIDE_URL&quot;</span>) is Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> target):
+        <span class="keyword">if</span> http.get(target) is Ok(<span class="keyword">var</span> response):
+            <span class="keyword">return</span> response.info.status
+    <span class="keyword">return</span> fallback</code></pre><div class="guide-result" data-source="/docs/snippets/read-status.void" data-input="0" data-expected="200">Input <strong>0</strong><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>Expected result <strong>200</strong></div></figure></section><p class="muted">Continue learning with <a href="/docs/async/">Async tasks</a> · <a href="/docs/files-paths/">File transfers</a>.</p><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Guide navigation"><a href="/docs/">← All guides</a></nav></article><nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#component">Encode one value</a><a href="#client">Own requests and responses</a><a href="#stream">Read incrementally</a><a href="#verification">Platform verification</a><a href="#try-it">Try the operation</a></nav></div></main><footer><div class="container footer-inner"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M2 5h12l13 23-6 11z"/><path fill="#6b779b" d="M17 5h11l-6 10z"/><path fill="#303b64" d="M31 5h11L29 28l-6-10z"/></svg><span>VOID <small>LANGUAGE</small></span></a><p>Native code. Clear intent.</p><div><a href="/docs/syntax/">Docs</a><a href="/docs/">All guides</a><a href="/github/">GitHub ↗</a></div></div></footer><div class="sr-only" id="announcement" role="status"></div></body></html>
